  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nAn expansive mid-level ridge centered over the Desert Southwest will \nremain the dominant weather feature through early next week, \nmaintaining hot and predominately dry conditions across South Texas. \nA weak disturbance skirting the eastern periphery of the ridge may \nbring isolated showers and thunderstorms Sunday, mainly across the \nCoastal Plains and Brush Country, though coverage has trended lower \nwith chances ranging from 15-20%. Otherwise, dry weather is expected \nthrough the remainder of the period.\n\nTemperatures will continue to climb through the weekend into early \nnext week with widespread triple-digit highs across the Brush \nCountry and Rio Grande Plains. Although slightly lower dewpoints \nhave reduced the areal coverage of advisory-level heat indices \nFriday and Saturday, moderate to major HeatRisk will remain common \nthis weekend with isolated areas of extreme HeatRisk persisting into \nearly next week. Continue to practice heat safety if spending time \noutdoors.",
